Relevant columns and possible usage  
"publication_date": derive the publication year (YYYY) and build 5‑year buckets; filter to 1960‑2020  
"country_code": keep only Canadian patents ('CA')  
"inventor": Variant array that lists inventors; need its size, and to keep only rows where this array contains ≥ 1 element  
"publication_number": unique identifier of a patent publication; use to count publications  
Optional / helper columns  
"kind_code": inspect types of Canadian publications if needed  
"application_kind": inspect high‑level kind (A, B, etc.)  
Conditions that will be useful  
"country_code" = 'CA'  
ARRAY_SIZE("inventor") > 0      -- has at least one inventor  
YEAR between 1960 and 2020       -- derived from "publication_date" (YYYYMMDD as INTEGER)  

Below are ten exploratory Snowflake SQL snippets, progressing from simple inspection to the final aggregation.  
Every query is wrapped with LIMIT 20 (except where noted) and all identifiers are double‑quoted.

```sql
-- 1) Description: Peek at a handful of Canadian publications and their raw inventor arrays
SELECT 
  "publication_number",
  "publication_date",
  "inventor",
  "kind_code"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS
WHERE "country_code" = 'CA'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Description: Distinct publication years we actually have for CA data
SELECT DISTINCT 
  FLOOR("publication_date"/10000) AS "pub_year"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS
WHERE "country_code" = 'CA'
ORDER BY "pub_year"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Description: Quick count of CA publications that list at least one inventor
SELECT 
  COUNT(*) AS "ca_with_inventor"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS
WHERE "country_code" = 'CA'
  AND ARRAY_SIZE("inventor") > 0
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Description: Flatten one record to look at individual inventor names
SELECT 
  p."publication_number",
  f.value::STRING AS "inventor_name"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."inventor") f
WHERE p."country_code" = 'CA'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Description: Sample inventor counts per patent
SELECT 
  "publication_number",
  ARRAY_SIZE("inventor") AS "inventor_cnt"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS
WHERE "country_code" = 'CA'
  AND ARRAY_SIZE("inventor") > 0
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Description: How many CA publications per 5‑year bucket (quick test without inventor filter)
SELECT 
  CONCAT(
    (FLOOR((pub_year-1960)/5)*5 + 1960), '-', 
    (FLOOR((pub_year-1960)/5)*5 + 1964)
  ) AS "five_year_period",
  COUNT(*) AS "pub_cnt"
FROM (
  SELECT 
    FLOOR("publication_date"/10000) AS pub_year
  FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS
  WHERE "country_code" = 'CA'
    AND "publication_date" BETWEEN 19600101 AND 20201231
) q
GROUP BY "five_year_period"
ORDER BY "five_year_period"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Description: Average number of inventors per CA patent for a single period (1960‑1964) – sanity check
SELECT 
  AVG(inv_cnt) AS "avg_inv_1960_64"
FROM (
  SELECT 
    ARRAY_SIZE("inventor") AS inv_cnt
  FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS
  WHERE "country_code" = 'CA'
    AND "publication_date" BETWEEN 19600101 AND 19641231
    AND ARRAY_SIZE("inventor") > 0
) x
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Description: Build a helper CTE that attaches inventor_count and 5‑year bucket to each CA publication
WITH ca_pub AS (
  SELECT 
    "publication_number",
    ARRAY_SIZE("inventor")              AS inv_cnt,
    FLOOR("publication_date"/10000)     AS pub_year
  FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS
  WHERE "country_code" = 'CA'
    AND "publication_date" BETWEEN 19600101 AND 20201231
    AND ARRAY_SIZE("inventor") > 0
)
SELECT * FROM ca_pub
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Description: Aggregate CA data by 5‑year period – preview without average
WITH ca_pub AS (
  SELECT 
    "publication_number",
    ARRAY_SIZE("inventor")              AS inv_cnt,
    FLOOR("publication_date"/10000)     AS pub_year
  FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS
  WHERE "country_code" = 'CA'
    AND "publication_date" BETWEEN 19600101 AND 20201231
    AND ARRAY_SIZE("inventor") > 0
)
SELECT 
  CONCAT(
    (FLOOR((pub_year-1960)/5)*5 + 1960), '-', 
    (FLOOR((pub_year-1960)/5)*5 + 1964)
  ) AS "five_year_period",
  COUNT(DISTINCT "publication_number")  AS "total_pubs",
  AVG(inv_cnt)                          AS "avg_inventors"
FROM ca_pub
GROUP BY "five_year_period"
ORDER BY "five_year_period"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--10) Description: Final query – average inventors per patent and total publication count 
--                 for Canadian patents, grouped by 5‑year intervals (1960‑2020)
WITH ca_pub AS (
  SELECT
    "publication_number",
    ARRAY_SIZE("inventor")              AS inv_cnt,
    FLOOR("publication_date"/10000)     AS pub_year
  FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS
  WHERE "country_code" = 'CA'
    AND "publication_date" BETWEEN 19600101 AND 20201231
    AND ARRAY_SIZE("inventor") > 0
)
SELECT
  CONCAT(
    (FLOOR((pub_year-1960)/5)*5 + 1960), '-', 
    (FLOOR((pub_year-1960)/5)*5 + 1964)
  )                                      AS "five_year_period",
  COUNT(DISTINCT "publication_number")    AS "total_publications",
  AVG(inv_cnt)                           AS "avg_inventors_per_patent"
FROM ca_pub
GROUP BY "five_year_period"
ORDER BY "five_year_period"
LIMIT 20;
```

